No, "yes" was my response to your question "Would you be able to confirm that this error does NOT... "

Branch GGIR2.0 s a development branch of GGIR, so it is expected that the output changes over time.
If you want more robust results wait for the release or go back to the CRAN version and adjust your analysis plan to what that version can handle.
As I mentioned before, do not expect much from part 5 in recordings where the accelerometer has hardly been worn for two consecutive days.

Vincent

